hadiths[1]{hadithnumber,text}:
"1444","Muhammad bin Rafi’ told us, Abdul Razzaq told us, Ibn Jurayj told us, Ata told me, on the authority of Jabir bin Abdullah, he said: I heard him. He says: “The Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, got up on the Day of Fitr and prayed. He began to pray before the sermon, then he addressed the people. When the Prophet of God had finished, May God’s prayers and peace be upon him, he descended and went to the women and reminded them while he was leaning on Bilal’s hand, and Bilal was spreading his garment to give the women charity,” I said. For giving: Zakat al-Fitr? He said: No, but it is charity that they give in charity at that time. The woman expels her semen, and they"
